IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rcrd-rebates`
IMPORT `rcrd-qa`

-- Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (rcrd-qa.l4): every exported
-- question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does not
-- hold (FALSE; for the partner, the two other values of `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`) and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. The partner's situation is read through helpers that
-- list every value with no OTHERWISE, so the trap of graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the pensioner or senior (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand
-- from the text (most taken from the baseline's own cases, rcrd-cases-rebates.l4, with the life's event id), and once
-- against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the partner and
-- the buyer or executor, the values are worked by hand from the text. The charges are ILLUSTRATIVE, as in the baseline;
-- facts the life does not state are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `unasked cards` IS A `My cards and circumstances`
ASSUME `an unasked home` IS A `My home`
ASSUME `an unasked basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility`
ASSUME `an unasked kind` IS A `Kind of charge`
ASSUME `unasked deferment circumstances` IS A `My deferment circumstances`
ASSUME `an unasked event` IS A `What happens to me`
ASSUME `an unasked partner event` IS A `What has happened to my partner`
ASSUME `an unasked claim` IS AN `Other claim on the land`
ASSUME `an unasked happening` IS A `What happened to the pensioner or the home`

`as the ratepayer` MEANS `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home`
`as the partner` MEANS `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home`
`as the buyer or executor` MEANS `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred`

