-- Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable?
-- s 45(2): further deferred while I live on there.
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has stopped living in our home` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
-- s 44(2)(c).
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has stopped living in our home` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- s 44(2)(c)(ii): my partner went into care.
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has stopped living in our home` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
-- s 45(2)(e).
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has stopped living in our home` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
-- s 44(2)(c)(ii) keeps them deferred whatever the order says of s 45(2).
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has stopped living in our home` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` `as the partner` `my partner has died` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
